  modified: in runBM;
	def runBM( ..., psudoNCountsForBM, psudoNCountsForhia, pseudoNCountsForProposedPia, psudoNCountsForKL, ... )
   The old versions correspond to the case , psudoNCountsForBM=0, psudoNCountsForhia=pseudoNCountsForProposedPia=psudoNCountsForKL=10
   except that in the present version fia and fijab are modified with psudoNCountsForBM in the calculation of KL.

   The best result will be obtained with psudoNCountsForBM=0, psudoNCountsForhia=pseudoNCountsForProposedPia=10, psudoNCountsForKL=1

  modified: In the case of no regularizatin, fiaWithPseudo, ..., can be employed instead of fia,... to avoid 0 counts in them.
            They are generated with pseudoNCountsForBM.
            If the regularization term is employed, pseudoNCountsForBM=0 should be employed.

    def iterateBMSteps( runBM1Step, interactions, fiaWithpseudo, fijabWithPseudo, faWithpseudo, ...
  modified: fiaQ and fijabQ for KLs are corrected with pseudoNCountsForKL.
    val ensembleKL = BM.calcKL(fiaWithPseudo, fijabWithPseudo, observedNP = Double.PositiveInfinity, pseudoNP = 0.0,
            ensembleAverages.pia, ensembleAverages.pijab, observedNQ = totalNSamples, pseudoNQ = pseudoNCountsKL,
            fiaWith0ReplacedBy1, fijabWith0ReplacedBy1 )
  modified: The mean and variance of energies of random sequences are calculated by using faWithPseudo.
  modified: val proposedPia = bayesianCorrection(this.fia, this.effectiveNConfigs, pseudoNCountsForProposedPia)
 
  where
    val (fiaWithPseudo, fijabWithPseudo) = bayesianCorrection(this.fia, this.fijab, this.effectiveNConfigs, pseudoNCountsForBM)
    val (fiaPWith0ReplacedBy1, fijabPWith0ReplacedBy1) = replace0By1ForKL(this.fia, this.fijab)
    val faWithPseudo = bayesianCorrection( this.fa, this.effectiveNConfigs * this.fia.size, pseudoNCountsForBM)



